#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198102 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "391bb8ae-88ba-520c-a5cf-7e2fa5474788" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Predicate Expressed in Plain English"}] :question/id #uuid "12d987fd-f966-522d-9370-48f7306930ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-12731" :question/problem "Write down $\\lnot P(x)$ given that\n![](images/76/76d3525ff67cd5e1d597c4bdbe7b056cefb528405f596fa19a02f7f19bd031ef.png)" :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$\\neg$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n![](images/c4/c4fcfc8fc10ea5b0cd7ee476d43cee41056e5c398aec7d4b9ca9f10dbc12c5d0.png) \n\nIn other words, $x$ is smaller than $10.$ Therefore, $\\neg P(x)$ means the following:\n![](images/92/92d40318f07563c997405d3f0002d479379bbce2cf8b88d7145e40fac1eb867c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198103 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198459 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "adbddf14-3aca-50dd-80f8-4146193c91ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of Predicate's Negation"}] :question/id #uuid "fcee0d41-9ff9-5f84-b8fe-73bfad36c7bb" :question/math-academy-id "e-12732" :question/problem "The shaded region below represents the truth set of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $\\mathbb{R}^2.$ Determine the region that represents the truth set of $\\neg P(x).$ \n\n![](images/cc/cc80d49abe6293acb1325035799dac833a9bcb8f485ed1f785f78c4e1f39b8be.png)" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $\\neg P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x){:}$\n\n$$\nT_{\\neg P} = \\overline{T}_P\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $\\neg P(x),$ we take all the points that belong to $U$ and do not lie in $T_p,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/86/86205c3b03c01581677b4fa877dae8c4ca743fe0ac0f1673ef504d548e8c785d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198111 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198458 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7943a26b-d4fa-5ce1-bc47-5ea4873fc367" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Predicate Expressed Using Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "adacf679-91a6-500f-b13a-18418d851d5b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12883" :question/problem "$\\qquad$ $x \\nleq \\sqrt{2}$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Write down $\\neg P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\qquad$ $x$ is not smaller than or equal to $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nThe symbol \"$\\neg$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\qquad$ It is not true that $x$ is not smaller than or equal to $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ *is* *smaller than or equal to* $\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, $\\neg P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\qquad$ $x\\leq \\sqrt{2}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198459 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "adbddf14-3aca-50dd-80f8-4146193c91ff" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of Predicate's Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86c2d878-acda-58c9-a9a3-45a8be215821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2, 3, 5, 7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194875} {:answer/id #uuid "a5255fa2-2f8d-53b9-8163-24715c5db8cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2, 4, 6, 8, 10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194876} {:answer/id #uuid "cf9ceec6-7a29-5081-b69b-91c944198acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{1, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194877} {:answer/id #uuid "0b410a78-f767-5568-ab2b-98dcde5467bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∅" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194878} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc5af4f-fa18-5a12-9d4b-405238a0c985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194879}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5dfc675b-4b61-5ea0-9a02-5e53514726dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194874}] :question/id #uuid "46ce81ed-7f98-523e-8348-7d75c19c5c70" :question/math-academy-id "q-171685" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set of positive integers between $1$ and $10$, inclusive:\n\n$P(x)$: $x$ is prime"}]}
